    <SocialSecurityTaxWithholdingCalculator client:load />
  </div>

    <div class="sstw-intro-guide" role="region" aria-label="How to use this calculator">
      <h2 class="sstw-intro-guide-title">How to Use This Calculator</h2>
      <ul class="sstw-intro-guide-list">
        <li><strong>What this tool estimates:</strong> Your monthly and annual federal tax deduction under official IRS Form W-4V rates (7%, 10%, 12%, 22%), your net monthly check deposit, and your projected April tax balance (refund or balance due).</li>
        <li><strong>What information you need:</strong> Your gross monthly (or annual) Social Security benefit and estimated other taxable retirement income (pensions, traditional IRA/401(k) withdrawals, wages, and any taxes already withheld elsewhere).</li>
        <li><strong>What the result means:</strong> The exact dollar reduction to your monthly check and how close that deduction brings your annual tax prepayments to matching your actual Form 1040 liability.</li>
        <li><strong>What the result does NOT mean:</strong> Withholding from Social Security is completely voluntary, not required by law; the SSA does not withhold state taxes via Form W-4V; and withholding does not alter your Medicare Part B premium.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>


